{# W3C SCXML G.7: <sce:action> native host dispatch.

   The call site is lowered ahead of the template by
   `forge::native_action::render` and stored on
   `action.native_action_rendered`, so this macro only places it at the
   caller's indent. It is deliberately ONE line: this backend's dispatcher
   hands each action the literal whitespace prefix its context needs, and a
   multi-line body would carry that prefix only on its first line. The
   arg-bearing form therefore binds the typed payload with `:=` inside the
   `if` that checks it is there — the same tag check the other five spell as
   a block. #}
{%- macro emit(action, indent, machine_name, model) -%}
{{ indent }}# W3C SCXML G.7: <sce:action name="{{ action.native_action_name }}">
{{ indent }}{{ action.native_action_rendered }}
{%- endmacro -%}
